 ("ul", ["Modern ones are **digital**, battery-run and use **heat sensors**; they measure when placed in contact with the body (under the tongue).",
  "Older **mercury thermometers** are being replaced because mercury is **toxic** and hard to dispose of if the thermometer breaks; digital ones are safer and easier to read.",
  "During COVID-19, **non-contact (infrared) thermometers** measured temperature without touching, reducing the spread of disease."]),
 ("h3", "Precautions while using a digital clinical thermometer"),
