 ("p", "Always check the range and smallest division of the thermometer before use."),
 ("h3", "Correct way of using a laboratory thermometer"),
 ("ul", ["The **bulb must not touch** the bottom or sides of the beaker.", "Hold the thermometer **vertically**, not tilted.", "Read the temperature **while the bulb is still in the water** (the column falls as soon as it is taken out).", "Keep the **eye in line** with the top of the liquid column.", "Wait until the column **stops rising**, but not so long that water cools.", "Handle with care (glass breaks) and do not hold by the bulb."]),
 ("p", "Differences in readings among students (e.g. boiling water at Shillong: 97.8 to 98.1 °C) show that **correct reading procedure was not followed by all**. Note: **temperature stays constant while ice melts and while water boils.** Experiments with boiling water are done only under the teacher's supervision."),
